  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light strikes a glass plate at an angle of $60^{\\circ}$. If the reflected and refracted rays are perpendicular to each other, the refractive index of glass is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YRWME",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SoUu1",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a9tLI",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wPEtH",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, angle of incidence is $60^{\\circ}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2016_phy_a8.png\">\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\\mu=\\frac{\\sin i}{\\sin r}\r\n$$\r\n$\\sin i=\\mu \\sin r$\r\nhere,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nr &=90-i \\\\\r\n\\sin i &=\\mu \\sin \\left(90^{\\circ}-i\\right)=\\mu \\cos i \\\\\r\n\\mu &=\\frac{\\sin i}{\\cos i}=\\tan i=\\tan 60^{\\circ} \\\\\r\n\\mu &=\\sqrt{3}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
